a="Check hearing and vision, interview the patient alone and then with a collateral informant, and use structured cognitive screening",
ae="Hearing and vision deficits can mimic cognitive impairment. Collateral information is essential because patients with dementia often lack insight. Interviewing the patient alone first respects autonomy and allows disclosure (including elder abuse). Structured tools (e.g., MoCA, and the IQCODE for informants) add validity.",
